WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.810
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.080 --> 00:07.120
(This series is a fictional work created for entertainment purposes.)

3
00:07.200 --> 00:08.240
(The characters, events, locations, organizations agencies, as well as religions, beliefs)

4
00:08.320 --> 00:09.280
(and symbols appearing in this story are presented for storytelling purposes only.)

5
00:09.360 --> 00:10.120
(No intention is made to reference, imply, criticize)

6
00:10.200 --> 00:10.960
(or allude to any individual, organization or religious group)

7
00:14.480 --> 00:15.480
(Chat)

8
00:15.560 --> 00:20.520
Hey

9
00:23.360 --> 00:24.200
(Seungwoo)

10
00:24.280 --> 00:27.000
I thought I wouldn't be able to live without you

11
00:27.080 --> 00:30.480
But look at me now

12
00:30.800 --> 00:32.360
I'm shining

13
00:32.439 --> 00:34.160
On nights when the sky turns against me

14
00:34.240 --> 00:37.200
When the rain falls inside my heart

15
00:37.280 --> 00:38.240
I play the same old songs

16
00:38.320 --> 00:40.560
That we used to listen to together

17
00:40.640 --> 00:42.320
Your picture is still right there

18
00:42.400 --> 00:44.120
But I'm not crying anymore

19
00:44.200 --> 00:45.120
I used to want you so badly

20
00:45.200 --> 00:46.800
Now I'm beginning to understand

21
00:46.880 --> 00:49.520
That love comes and go

22
00:49.600 --> 00:51.560
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

23
00:51.640 --> 00:52.480
But in the end

24
00:52.560 --> 00:55.960
It was just my heart learning how to move on

25
00:57.240 --> 00:59.640
I used to say "Can't live without you"

26
00:59.720 --> 01:02.280
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

27
01:02.360 --> 01:03.480
I’m looking so good

28
01:03.560 --> 01:05.960
Damn I don’t even try to do

29
01:23.080 --> 01:24.520
You must choose.

30
01:31.200 --> 01:32.400
What do you mean?

31
01:32.479 --> 01:33.920
You must choose

32
01:34.479 --> 01:35.720
and make good decisions

33
01:36.080 --> 01:38.479
both in work and in love.

34
01:38.560 --> 01:40.680
If it's about work, I can understand that.

35
01:41.200 --> 01:42.600
But when it comes to love,

36
01:42.680 --> 01:44.120
there’s no way I’ll change my mind.

37
01:44.200 --> 01:45.080
But

38
01:45.160 --> 01:48.000
you will let love get involved with work.

39
01:55.960 --> 01:57.800
There’s absolutely no way that will happen.

40
01:58.840 --> 02:00.160
Just be careful then.

41
02:00.240 --> 02:01.920
Because one single mistake

42
02:03.760 --> 02:05.680
will cause everything to fall apart.

43
02:14.720 --> 02:17.600
We spent 1 year developing this product.

44
02:17.680 --> 02:20.040
And to solve the pain point of regular sunscreen

45
02:20.120 --> 02:21.440
where you have to squeeze a tube,

46
02:21.520 --> 02:22.600
you just open the cap and

47
02:22.680 --> 02:24.360
you can spray it directly onto your face,

48
02:24.440 --> 02:26.200
and it can also be applied over makeup.

49
02:26.280 --> 02:28.400
Our formula contains mineral oil

50
02:28.480 --> 02:30.920
to add moisture to the skin of your face.

51
02:31.320 --> 02:32.920
And our product design emphasizes

52
02:33.000 --> 02:34.360
a distinctive bottle color,

53
02:34.800 --> 02:35.640
just picking it up

54
02:35.720 --> 02:37.680
is enough to make our product memorable.

55
02:37.760 --> 02:39.079
Doesn’t this color

56
02:39.160 --> 02:40.800
look a little strange?

57
02:41.640 --> 02:43.320
We want to create brand recognition.

58
02:43.840 --> 02:45.680
First impressions are crucial.

59
02:45.760 --> 02:47.240
A bottle color like this

60
02:47.320 --> 02:48.160
draws people’s attention

61
02:48.240 --> 02:49.640
and makes it easy to share.

62
02:50.040 --> 02:51.840
I think this idea is quite interesting.

63
02:59.960 --> 03:02.720
Everyone, our team has a problem.

64
03:11.800 --> 03:13.840
Their idea is pretty brilliant though.

65
03:15.720 --> 03:16.560
Then...

66
03:17.000 --> 03:19.520
let’s quickly find the weaknesses of this product.

67
03:19.600 --> 03:20.960
I will absolutely not let Team B

68
03:21.040 --> 03:22.720
beat our Team A.

69
03:26.720 --> 03:27.960
Here it is.

70
03:28.040 --> 03:29.160
Our team’s product.

71
03:29.240 --> 03:31.079
I’ve already updated everything.

72
03:32.840 --> 03:34.720
This is the latest update, right?

73
03:34.800 --> 03:37.040
Yes, and it’s all compiled together.

74
03:42.160 --> 03:43.680
And I think

75
03:43.760 --> 03:46.720
this product can become a top seller too

76
03:46.800 --> 03:47.880
because not many companies

77
03:47.960 --> 03:49.560
have a formula like this yet.

78
03:50.079 --> 03:51.520
And when do you plan to launch?

79
03:51.600 --> 03:53.120
Around three months.

80
03:56.400 --> 03:58.840
Excuse me, it's Cathy Doll company.

81
04:01.200 --> 04:03.200
When you say there’s no competition,

82
04:03.600 --> 04:05.200
where did you check that information from?

83
04:06.120 --> 04:09.000
From reliable industry reports.

84
04:09.440 --> 04:10.680
Then why is there information

85
04:10.760 --> 04:12.000
that Cathy Doll is currently

86
04:12.080 --> 04:13.520
developing this same product?

87
04:17.160 --> 04:18.839
Where did that information come from?

88
04:21.200 --> 04:23.040
The information came from Team A.

89
04:24.720 --> 04:26.520
Then go call Team A’s leader in.

90
04:34.600 --> 04:36.600
You are at risk of losing your job

91
04:36.680 --> 04:37.960
and your reputation.

92
04:38.840 --> 04:40.360
Compose yourself well

93
04:40.960 --> 04:42.880
and you will get through it.

94
05:01.080 --> 05:03.680
How confident are you in the information you found?

95
05:04.280 --> 05:05.520
I'm very confident.

96
05:05.600 --> 05:06.640
because Team A

97
05:06.720 --> 05:08.520
has been tracking competitor companies’ information,

98
05:09.160 --> 05:10.880
and regarding this particular product,

99
05:10.960 --> 05:13.920
there is clear information in the industry report.

100
05:20.480 --> 05:21.600
May I?

101
05:26.320 --> 05:27.240
Here you go.

102
05:31.880 --> 05:32.920
Here you go.

103
05:52.720 --> 05:54.440
But this is just a market trend

104
05:54.800 --> 05:56.200
it hasn’t actually been produced yet.

105
05:56.280 --> 05:58.200
But a contact who works at Cathy Doll,

106
05:58.280 --> 05:59.640
someone I’ve worked with before,

107
05:59.720 --> 06:01.560
told me that this product

108
06:01.640 --> 06:03.320
will be released next month.

109
06:07.160 --> 06:08.040
Even if they release first,

110
06:08.120 --> 06:09.360
if our product is truly good,

111
06:09.440 --> 06:10.920
customers will still choose us.

112
06:11.560 --> 06:13.800
When you didn’t even know about their product at all,

113
06:14.320 --> 06:16.200
how can you be confident yours will be better?

114
06:22.280 --> 06:24.480
VEGA lab has never followed behind anyone.

115
06:26.200 --> 06:28.280
I’m going to have to reconsider you lot.

116
06:52.920 --> 06:54.920
I won’t beat around the bush.

117
06:55.520 --> 06:58.640
Team B has only three months left.

118
07:00.160 --> 07:02.000
If there are still no results,

119
07:02.080 --> 07:03.480
I’ll have to let you go.

120
07:04.360 --> 07:05.840
I’ll take full responsibility.

121
07:06.360 --> 07:08.040
I mean the entire team.

122
07:49.159 --> 07:50.600
This lane is brutal.

123
07:51.480 --> 07:52.840
But I'm getting ganked right now.

124
07:52.920 --> 07:54.159
Can I get some support?

125
07:54.240 --> 07:55.760
Yeah, hold on.

126
07:55.840 --> 07:57.080
No, play properly.

127
07:58.960 --> 08:00.120
Hey!

128
08:01.920 --> 08:02.960
Be careful!

129
08:03.040 --> 08:04.160
Yeah, yeah.

130
08:05.280 --> 08:06.360
Yeah, yeah.

131
08:06.440 --> 08:07.840
Attack them.

132
08:14.840 --> 08:16.320
Use Troy for magic resist first,

133
08:16.400 --> 08:18.160
the other side has mages,

134
08:18.240 --> 08:19.440
they're strong.

135
08:27.960 --> 08:29.600
You're teaching so well,

136
08:31.080 --> 08:32.760
is the tutoring fee expensive?

137
08:34.360 --> 08:36.080
Depends on who I’m teaching.

138
08:37.720 --> 08:39.159
Some people get it for free.

139
08:49.400 --> 08:50.360
Whoa!

140
08:51.200 --> 08:53.240
How about that? Pretty cool right?

141
08:53.560 --> 08:54.720
We even won.

142
08:54.800 --> 08:56.200
See? Got MVP too.

143
08:56.280 --> 08:57.520
Cool or what?

144
08:58.840 --> 09:01.800
My, are you this good at everything then?

145
09:05.280 --> 09:06.920
Damn! I’m heading out!

146
09:07.360 --> 09:08.560
I have to submit work to the professor.

147
09:08.640 --> 09:09.920
Lock up when you leave. See you.

148
09:10.000 --> 09:10.840
Wait!

149
09:10.920 --> 09:12.000
Wait!

150
09:21.120 --> 09:22.240
Then...

151
09:24.080 --> 09:25.160
shall we...

152
09:26.720 --> 09:28.520
keep playing, just the two of us?

153
09:41.600 --> 09:43.000
(Jeno)

154
09:46.240 --> 09:47.800
(Jeno)

155
10:02.880 --> 10:03.880
Nueng.

156
10:03.960 --> 10:05.920
I saw that you haven’t had lunch yet,

157
10:06.000 --> 10:08.040
so I bought you some snacks.

158
10:08.560 --> 10:09.880
And what about love?

159
10:18.440 --> 10:20.240
The people who enter your life will be

160
10:21.400 --> 10:23.640
associated with the number one throughout.

161
10:26.800 --> 10:27.880
Chat.

162
10:29.560 --> 10:30.640
Chat.

163
10:30.720 --> 10:31.800
Huh?

164
10:32.840 --> 10:35.240
Mira shouldn’t have done that to you.

165
10:35.920 --> 10:37.280
Because I think your work

166
10:37.360 --> 10:38.680
was genuinely good.

167
10:42.320 --> 10:43.640
I made the mistake myself.

168
10:46.360 --> 10:47.960
Sucking up to Chat,

169
10:48.840 --> 10:51.040
thinking of working across both teams, huh?

170
10:52.800 --> 10:54.560
Come on Chat, let’s go eat,

171
10:54.640 --> 10:55.520
the team is waiting.

172
10:56.200 --> 10:58.400
About working across two teams,

173
10:59.240 --> 11:00.480
if you don’t perform well,

174
11:00.560 --> 11:01.600
it’s not guaranteed.

175
11:01.680 --> 11:03.160
Your team passed,

176
11:03.720 --> 11:05.960
but that doesn’t mean you’re better than Team B.

177
11:08.760 --> 11:10.120
Let's not fight.

178
11:10.760 --> 11:12.440
We’re all in the same company.

179
11:13.920 --> 11:16.440
Chat, why do you even care about them?

180
11:16.760 --> 11:19.440
They’re always messing with us.

181
11:21.280 --> 11:22.200
I’ll head out first.

182
11:22.280 --> 11:23.600
maybe someone around here

183
11:24.080 --> 11:25.520
will cool down a bit.

184
11:26.840 --> 11:27.840
Chat,

185
11:28.200 --> 11:30.040
please don’t forget to enjoy your snacks.

186
11:30.120 --> 11:31.040
Mmm.

187
11:34.840 --> 11:37.240
Easy there.

188
11:59.960 --> 12:04.000
Congratulations to Team B!

189
12:09.560 --> 12:10.800
Don't tell me...

190
12:12.440 --> 12:14.240
You guys didn't pass again.

191
12:15.040 --> 12:17.400
If I pass, will I be in this condition, sis?

192
12:19.440 --> 12:20.600
It’s alright. Come on,

193
12:20.680 --> 12:21.880
I’ll treat you to a meal today.

194
12:22.640 --> 12:23.680
Come, come.

195
12:24.800 --> 12:26.480
What should we eat today?

196
12:27.320 --> 12:28.720
Come on, take a seat.

197
12:29.040 --> 12:30.440
I have no appetite, sis.

198
12:30.800 --> 12:32.360
Huh? Why is that?

199
12:38.000 --> 12:41.400
If our team’s project doesn’t pass in these three months,

200
12:41.480 --> 12:42.640
the whole team has to go.

201
12:43.000 --> 12:44.120
Huh?

202
12:52.160 --> 12:53.000
Jeez.

203
12:54.320 --> 12:57.320
So Team B better start preparing to find new jobs then.

204
13:00.680 --> 13:01.840
You’re so nosy

205
13:01.920 --> 13:04.560
about other people’s business, Namwan!

206
13:04.640 --> 13:07.760
Who knows, she might come buy your drink shop!

207
13:07.840 --> 13:08.720
Oh really?

208
13:08.800 --> 13:11.520
Maybe sell your food better first, auntie!

209
13:13.600 --> 13:14.880
Go bankrupt already!

210
13:14.960 --> 13:16.200
Use the time you spend talking

211
13:16.280 --> 13:18.440
to go find yourself a new job too!

212
13:21.920 --> 13:24.040
You don’t have to go find new jobs anywhere.

213
13:28.160 --> 13:29.840
You can come work with me.

214
13:30.360 --> 13:31.920
Team A has a lot of work,

215
13:32.000 --> 13:33.680
we happen to need more people.

216
13:36.040 --> 13:38.000
It’s not that you’re not good,

217
13:38.080 --> 13:39.200
it’s just that

218
13:39.600 --> 13:41.920
your leader isn’t good enough.

219
13:42.000 --> 13:44.240
Choose the wrong team and this is what happens!

220
13:48.920 --> 13:50.520
There are still three months.

221
13:50.600 --> 13:51.720
There’s no way

222
13:51.800 --> 13:53.680
I’m letting Team B get fired.

223
13:53.760 --> 13:55.360
You seem confident.

224
13:56.440 --> 13:59.000
Let’s hope that confidence of a team leader

225
13:59.640 --> 14:01.880
doesn’t end up causing trouble for your team members.

226
14:02.720 --> 14:04.080
We’re not going to be in trouble.

227
14:04.520 --> 14:05.880
We’ll stick around

228
14:05.960 --> 14:07.960
and be a thorn in the side of people who love to bark

229
14:08.720 --> 14:11.600
aren’t you tired of barking like a mad dog?

230
14:12.040 --> 14:13.480
You’re the one who’s barking.

231
14:13.560 --> 14:16.640
Oh acting all high and mighty saying you won’t be in trouble

232
14:16.720 --> 14:19.760
just wait until you actually get fired.

233
14:19.840 --> 14:21.280
You’ll be speechless,

234
14:21.680 --> 14:24.000
scrambling to find a new job barely in time.

235
14:24.640 --> 14:25.960
That’s enough, Tommy.

236
14:26.440 --> 14:27.840
Whatever you want to say,

237
14:27.920 --> 14:29.880
save my old friend's face a little.

238
14:33.400 --> 14:34.480
But if

239
14:36.000 --> 14:38.000
you do end up getting fired,

240
14:38.720 --> 14:40.000
you can tell me.

241
14:40.640 --> 14:42.600
I’ll go talk to Ms. Nichakorn for you.

242
14:58.040 --> 14:59.600
He doesn’t care about you.

243
15:02.520 --> 15:05.600
Team A and Team B can’t be friends.

244
15:06.240 --> 15:08.440
But you and I, we used to be friends.

245
15:09.080 --> 15:10.000
Used to be.

246
15:10.520 --> 15:12.800
But it ended the day we became rivals.

247
15:13.160 --> 15:14.320
Besides,

248
15:14.920 --> 15:16.120
what you’re hoping for,

249
15:16.600 --> 15:18.040
it will never happen

250
15:19.040 --> 15:21.440
And do you even know what I’m hoping for?

251
15:21.880 --> 15:23.680
I could tell what you were thinking

252
15:24.280 --> 15:25.600
even from the moon.

253
15:25.680 --> 15:27.200
If you already know then good,

254
15:27.920 --> 15:29.280
because if I want something,

255
15:29.840 --> 15:30.880
I will get it.

256
15:32.920 --> 15:34.080
Go ahead and try.

257
15:58.440 --> 16:00.400
At least only work fails,

258
16:00.480 --> 16:02.160
but my love life is still okay.

259
16:03.480 --> 16:07.160
(Jeno, Chat)

260
16:12.800 --> 16:14.720
(Nice to meet you)

261
16:30.120 --> 16:34.480
(Jeno, Chat)

262
16:35.080 --> 16:37.120
This is your surprise?

263
16:39.080 --> 16:40.160
Yes.

264
16:40.440 --> 16:42.240
today is our anniversary,

265
16:42.800 --> 16:44.760
so I wanted to do something

266
16:46.240 --> 16:48.800
to show you how much I love you.

267
16:48.880 --> 16:50.160
Just a lock?

268
16:59.760 --> 17:02.560
Do you know that in Korea there’s a belief that

269
17:03.200 --> 17:05.079
if you lock a padlock with someone,

270
17:05.680 --> 17:07.440
it will make your love strong

271
17:08.839 --> 17:10.359
and you’ll never break up?

272
17:15.760 --> 17:16.880
Do you believe in that?

273
17:20.079 --> 17:23.160
I’m just scared you’ll break up with me.

274
17:28.520 --> 17:29.360
Jeno.

275
17:30.400 --> 17:32.800
You know, you are my first love?

276
17:35.360 --> 17:36.800
No matter what happens,

277
17:36.880 --> 17:38.800
there’s no way I’d ever leave you.

278
17:40.960 --> 17:42.080
You said it now,

279
17:42.960 --> 17:44.360
if you leave me,

280
17:44.720 --> 17:46.200
I have nowhere to go.

281
17:56.480 --> 17:57.600
Your hand.

282
18:00.920 --> 18:01.800
Let's go.

283
18:07.840 --> 18:11.920
Let me lock it, so we love each other forever.

284
18:16.520 --> 18:18.280
Just don’t cheat on me and that’s enough.

285
18:27.960 --> 18:30.240
I’m hungry. Let’s go find something to eat.

286
18:38.760 --> 18:40.200
In place of a promise.

287
20:08.520 --> 20:09.600
Jeno.

288
20:11.680 --> 20:12.520
Yes?

289
20:12.600 --> 20:14.120
I bought you noodles.

290
20:16.120 --> 20:18.400
Come eat while it’s hot, it won’t taste good later.

291
20:19.440 --> 20:20.400
Yes.

292
20:38.800 --> 20:40.280
How was your day?

293
20:42.800 --> 20:43.760
Sorry.

294
20:43.840 --> 20:45.320
It's all wet, Jeno.

295
20:46.640 --> 20:48.200
Not playing games today?

296
20:54.760 --> 20:55.800
I will.

297
20:56.520 --> 20:57.760
And I’m planning to enter a competition

298
20:57.840 --> 20:59.560
and bring back first prize for you.

299
21:00.880 --> 21:03.240
The people who enter your life will be

300
21:03.760 --> 21:05.800
associated with the number one throughout.

301
21:10.320 --> 21:11.720
If you get first place what do you get?

302
21:11.800 --> 21:13.720
Wouldn’t it be better to focus on studying?

303
21:15.560 --> 21:17.240
Studying has its place.

304
21:17.840 --> 21:19.440
But games can earn income too.

305
21:19.520 --> 21:20.520
Look.

306
21:21.960 --> 21:23.320
But it’s not stable.

307
21:25.040 --> 21:26.640
Then what is stability?

308
21:28.800 --> 21:31.720
Is it living my life the way you think is correct?

309
21:32.840 --> 21:34.800
I’m not just playing games mindlessly.

310
21:40.280 --> 21:41.320
Jeno.

311
21:42.200 --> 21:43.240
Jeno.

312
21:46.160 --> 21:48.200
What’s wrong? I’m just worried about you.

313
21:51.920 --> 21:53.280
Worried about what?

314
21:59.000 --> 22:00.000
What’s that mark?

315
22:01.840 --> 22:02.960
I was just itchy.

316
22:09.000 --> 22:10.200
Was it very itchy?

317
22:10.800 --> 22:12.200
That’s clearly a hickey.

318
22:18.960 --> 22:20.720
Tell me, who did you sleep with?

319
22:21.400 --> 22:22.960
I didn’t sleep with anyone.

320
22:24.400 --> 22:26.120
Do you think I’m stupid?

321
22:33.280 --> 22:34.280
Hey!

322
22:34.360 --> 22:35.360
Hey!

323
22:40.440 --> 22:41.920
How could you do this?

324
22:43.840 --> 22:44.920
Chat.

325
22:46.440 --> 22:48.120
Where did I go wrong?

326
22:49.960 --> 22:51.440
The three years we’ve been together,

327
22:51.520 --> 22:52.840
did they mean nothing to you at all?

328
22:55.440 --> 22:56.520
Chat.

